Description: Orbit's firewall: incoming connections dropped, each service opening its own
 Loads one nftables table, inet orbit, and leaves every other alone
 (Docker's, libvirt's, Tailscale's): what comes in is dropped but for
 answers to this machine, the loopback, ICMP, its own VMs and containers,
 and the ports each service's file opens, to the local network and the
 tunnels only. Each Orbit service brings its file to
 /usr/share/orbit/firewall.d; this machine's own go in
 /etc/orbit/firewall.d. Installed on a machine already in use, it keeps
 what the machine already served open to the local network. orbit-firewall
 status says what is open.
Section: net
Depends: nftables, iproute2
